sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-paulistorum-turing-wavelength-s0> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-paulistorum-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-paulistorum-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Drosophila paulistorum Schnakenberg ocellar stripe at 2.4 µm (Pass 2) — MorphoEval overall 88.3/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 2 multiplies both diffusivities by 0.478965 so argmax σ(k) lies at 2.417 µm (σ=3.13). A 9-point Du sweep, each point seeded with its integer maximum-growth mode, recovers that wavelength from the activator FFT at Pearson r=0.989 (RMSE 0.064 µm). The nominal patch (6 waves, 14.502 µm) measures 2.417 µm. Equal diffusion (d=1) drops the activator standard deviation by a factor of about 1e-5. The Haars 2018 male is segmented (foreground 0.300, coherency 0.632, circularity 0.597). The growth GIF is 12 frames at 640×480; last-frame CV similarity against the photograph is 85.9. Image fitness using the Pass 2 subscores is 85.9. Versus the catalog predecessor D. orena (89.44 µm) the detail mode packs 37 times (remainder 11 nm); versus D. persimilis (116.7 µm) it packs 48 times (remainder 684 nm). All three ages are 0 Ma. Overall 88.3/100 (faithfulness 88.1, reproducibility 88.7); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 9a9d6408; environment: python 3.12.3, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.18.1, matplotlib 3.11.2, Pillow 13.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 91, Morphological realism / specimen match 84, Parameter expressivity 90, Morphometric validation 90, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 88, Reproducibility package 88. Output judged: docs/media/drosophila_paulistorum_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-paulistorum-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 9a9d6408, image/png, 435973 B, 1740×912 px, artifact_sha256 26d4992383a6d270eb32a0d049e22264a9afc1f82990d04f9cbf33c6da9acf4d (sha256 26d4992383a6d270eb32a0d049e22264a9afc1f82990d04f9cbf33c6da9acf4d), spec_fingerprint 59419ebb8a88efc4005d1cc11aab51778bad8613c26ac834a4d86676d99742f1. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 59419ebb8a88efc4005d1cc11aab51778bad8613c26ac834a4d86676d99742f1; artifact_sha256: 26d4992383a6d270eb32a0d049e22264a9afc1f82990d04f9cbf33c6da9acf4d; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/drosophila_paulistorum_turing_wavelength_s0/README.md=b770bcff5173b0a0..., datasets/drosophila_paulistorum_turing_wavelength_s0/drosophila_paulistorum_male_haars_2018.png=e01e60e633f99ef1..., datasets/drosophila_paulistorum_turing_wavelength_s0/drosophila_paulistorum_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=39b5153e4682ffee..., datasets/drosophila_paulistorum_turing_wavelength_s0/paper_citations.bib=5c00ca3d9a631902..., datasets/drosophila_paulistorum_turing_wavelength_s0/scout_manifest.json=a859ae40d3f79e52...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-27-drosophila-paulistorum-turing-wavelength-s0-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Dobzhansky & Spassky 1959: D. paulistorum is a willistoni-group cluster of incipient semispecies. Holocene, 0 Ma. | Turing 1952 and Maini, Painter & Chau 1997: finite-k instability conditions (trace, determinant, diffusivity ratio). | Schnakenberg 1979: the activator-inhibitor kinetics. | Haars 2018: the CC BY-SA 4.0 adult male photograph used as the habitus.; reconstructed_in_script: Diffusivity magnitude 0.478965 chosen so the maximum of σ(k), not only the determinant stationary point, equals 2.417 µm. | Nine-point Du sweep and equal-diffusion ablation on a periodic intra-ocellar patch. | Packing counts against the catalog neighbors D. orena and D. persimilis.; transfer_boundary: The 2.417 µm length is the assigned subcellular rung, on the order of a Drosophila rhabdomere diameter. It is not a published paulistorum morphometric. | Gompel et al. 2005 is a wing-pigment citation only.; does_not_claim: That Dobzhansky & Spassky measured a 2.4 µm Turing wavelength. | That the catalog order orena → paulistorum → persimilis is a fossil lineage. | That the low-amplitude stripe impress on the habitus is an electron micrograph of ommochrome granules. | A signed nanopublication. No local nanopub profile was present.." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:hasScore "0.883"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 (primary loop assessor)" ;
        dct:identifier "grok-4.7" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://github.com/fractastical> ;
        foaf:homepage <https://x.ai> .
}

